<h2 class="uncap" style="font-weight: 400;">
  A marketplace listing's serial matches a stolen registration
</h2>

<p>
  The <%= @listed_bike.type %> below is listed for sale on the marketplace, and
  its serial matches a registration that's reported stolen. Nothing was blocked
  automatically: the listing is still up.
</p>

<p>
  Please check whether they're the same <%= @stolen_bike.type %>. Serials are
  compared in segments, so a partial match can be a coincidence.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>For sale:</strong> <%= @listed_bike.title_string %>, serial
  <code><%= @listed_bike.serial_number %></code>
  <br>
  <%= link_to "Admin page", admin_bike_url(@listed_bike) %> &middot;
  <%= link_to "Public page", bike_url(@listed_bike) %>
  <% if @marketplace_listing.present? %>
    &middot;
    <%= link_to "Marketplace listing (admin)", admin_marketplace_listing_url(@marketplace_listing) %>
  <% end %>
</p>

<p>
  <strong>Stolen:</strong> <%= @stolen_bike.title_string %>, serial
  <code><%= @stolen_bike.serial_number %></code>
  <br>
  <%= link_to "Admin page", admin_bike_url(@stolen_bike) %> &middot;
  <%= link_to "Public page", bike_url(@stolen_bike) %>
</p>

<p style="color: #555;">
  If they aren't the same, you can ignore this email; it won't be sent again for
  this pair.
</p>
